    [
        {
            "type": "header",
            "bbox": [
                0.447,
                0.042,
                0.553,
                0.056
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "WT/DS629/R"
        },
        {
            "type": "page_number",
            "bbox": [
                0.482,
                0.069,
                0.517,
                0.082
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "121"
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph_title",
            "bbox": [
                0.116,
                0.1,
                0.635,
                0.115
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "7.3.4.5 China's claim under Article X:3(a) of the GATT 1994"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.128,
                0.882,
                0.157
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "7.527. China claims that Türkiye has acted inconsistently with Article X:3(a) of the GATT 1994 because it has not administered the IPLS in a uniform, impartial and reasonable manner. \\( ^{651} \\)",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.168,
                0.885,
                0.248
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "7.528. As adjudicators have pointed out in prior cases, the obligations in Article X of the GATT 1994 govern the publication and administration of measures, rather than the substantive content of measures. \\( ^{652} \\)  Where the substantive content of a measure has been found to be inconsistent with obligations in the GATT 1994, additional findings relating to the administration of that measure will in principle be superfluous and findings under Article X are unlikely to be necessary or useful in resolving the matter. \\( ^{653} \\)",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.26,
                0.883,
                0.302
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "7.529. Having found that the IPLS is inconsistent with Article III:4, we do not believe that an additional finding whether the manner in which Türkiye has administered the IPLS is inconsistent with Article X:3(a) would be necessary to resolve the dispute before us.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.313,
                0.883,
                0.355
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "7.530. Accordingly, we do not consider it necessary to make findings under Article X:3(a) of the GATT 1994 in addition to our findings under Article III:4. We therefore exercise judicial economy over China's claim under Article X:3(a).",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph_title",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.366,
                0.51,
                0.381
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "8 CONCLUSIONS AND RECOMMENDATION(S)"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.395,
                0.709,
                0.409
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "8.1. For the reasons set forth in this Report, the Panel concludes as follows:",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.162,
                0.421,
                0.882,
                0.449
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "a. With regard to the additional duties in their current amended version enacted through Presidential Decision No. 10436 of 22 September 2025:",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.191,
                0.462,
                0.883,
                0.49
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "i. China has not made a prima facie case that the additional duties on internal combustion engine vehicles are inconsistent with Article II:1(b) of the GATT 1994;",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.191,
                0.502,
                0.883,
                0.557
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "ii. the additional duties on electric vehicles and on those hybrid vehicles that would have been classified under the 34 tariff lines listed in Table 3 in paragraph 7.73 above, prior to the introduction of HS 2017, are inconsistent with Article II:1(b) of the GATT 1994, because they exceed tariff bindings in Türkiye's schedule;",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.192,
                0.568,
                0.884,
                0.635
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "iii. the additional duties on electric vehicles and on those hybrid vehicles that would have been classified under the 34 tariff lines listed in Table 3 in paragraph 7.73 above, prior to the introduction of HS 2017, are inconsistent with Article II:1(a) of the GATT 1994, because they accord less favourable treatment than that provided for in Türkiye's schedule;",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.192,
                0.647,
                0.883,
                0.69
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "iv. the additional duties on those hybrid vehicles that would not have been classified under the 34 tariff lines listed in Table 3 in paragraph 7.73 above, prior to the introduction of HS 2017, are not inconsistent with Articles II:1(b) and II:1(a) of the GATT 1994;",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.192,
                0.7,
                0.883,
                0.742
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "v. the inconsistency with Articles II:1(b) and II:1(a) of the GATT 1994 is not justified under Article XX(b), because Türkiye has not demonstrated the existence of a risk to human, animal or plant life or health;",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.192,
                0.754,
                0.883,
                0.796
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "vi. the inconsistency with Articles II:1(b) and II:1(a) of the GATT 1994 is not justified under Article XX(g), because Türkiye has not demonstrated that the additional duties relate to the conservation of natural resources;",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.192,
                0.807,
                0.884,
                0.836
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "vii. the additional duties are inconsistent with Article I:1 of the GATT 1994 because by exempting EVs and other vehicles from Türkiye's RTA partners from these duties,",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "page_footnote",
            "bbox": [
                0.161,
                0.855,
                0.827,
                0.869
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "\\( ^{651} \\)  China's first written submission, paras. 230-251; second written submission, paras. 219-245."
        },
        {
            "type": "page_footnote",
            "bbox": [
                0.161,
                0.867,
                0.519,
                0.881
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "\\( ^{652} \\)  Appellate Body Report, EC – Poultry, para. 115."
        },
        {
            "type": "page_footnote",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.879,
                0.861,
                0.916
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "\\( ^{653} \\)  Panel Reports, Argentina – Import Measures, para. 6.305; Turkey – Pharmaceutical Products (EU), para. 7.251; Russia – Traffic in Transit, paras. 7.200-7.201; Peru – Agricultural Products, para. 7.501; and Russia – Railway Equipment, para. 7.939."
        },
