    [
        {
            "type": "header",
            "bbox": [
                0.447,
                0.042,
                0.553,
                0.057
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "WT/DS629/R"
        },
        {
            "type": "page_number",
            "bbox": [
                0.482,
                0.068,
                0.518,
                0.081
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "122"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.219,
                0.1,
                0.882,
                0.13
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Türkiye fails to accord to products from China an advantage accorded to the like product originating from Türkiye's RTA partners;",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.192,
                0.141,
                0.882,
                0.195
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "viii. the inconsistency with Article I:1 of the GATT 1994 is justified under Article XXIV with respect to the exemption from the additional duties of vehicles from Türkiye's RTA partners listed in Presidential Decision No. 10436 except for vehicles from Venezuela; and",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.192,
                0.206,
                0.883,
                0.249
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "ix. the inconsistency with Article I:1 of the GATT 1994 with respect to the exemption from the additional duties of vehicles from Venezuela is not justified under Article XXIV, under the Enabling Clause, or under Articles XX(b) and (g).",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph_title",
            "bbox": [
                0.164,
                0.26,
                0.386,
                0.275
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "b. With regard to the IPLS:"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.191,
                0.288,
                0.884,
                0.356
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "i. the IPLS is inconsistent with Article III:4 of the GATT 1994 because it accords less favourable treatment to EVs and ERHVs from China than the treatment accorded to the like products from Türkiye with respect to the Service Stations, Certificate of Competence, Call Centre, Authorized Representative, and Battery Commitment Requirements, and with respect to the mechanism to enforce these requirements;",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.192,
                0.366,
                0.883,
                0.422
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "ii. the inconsistency with Article III:4 of the GATT 1994 is not justified under Article XX(d) because Türkiye has not demonstrated that each of the IPLS requirements and the IPLS enforcement mechanism are taken \"to secure compliance with\" the Law on Consumer Protection and the Type Approval Regulation;",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.192,
                0.433,
                0.883,
                0.474
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "iii. we exercise judicial economy over China's claims that the IPLS is inconsistent with Articles I:1, X:3(a), and XI:1 of the GATT 1994, and with Article 2.1 of the TRIMs Agreement.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.486,
                0.884,
                0.554
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "8.2. Under Article 3.8 of the DSU, in cases where there is an infringement of the obligations assumed under a covered agreement, the action is considered prima facie to constitute a case of nullification or impairment. We conclude that, to the extent that the measures at issue are inconsistent with the GATT 1994, they have nullified or impaired benefits accruing to China under that agreement.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.565,
                0.883,
                0.594
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "8.3. Pursuant to Article 19.1 of the DSU, we recommend that Türkiye bring its measures into conformity with its obligations under the GATT 1994.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
